<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="QueryFlag: Run a query on selected text" id="Work-with-QueryFlag">

    <primary-label ref="queryflag"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter,procedure" depth="2"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Run: right-click the selection and select <ui-path>Query Flag in DB | &lt;template name&gt;</ui-path></p>
        <p>Requires: a template whose data source is available in the project</p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Select a value in the editor and run a saved QueryFlag template with it from the context menu.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Select a value in the editor and run a template with it from the context menu.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Run QueryFlag templates on the text you select in the editor of JetBrains IDEs: QueryFlag fills in the value, runs the query, and shows the results.</web-summary>

    <p>
        Select a value in the editor, for example a feature flag key or a customer e-mail in your code,
        and run a saved query with it without typing the query yourself.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Before you begin" id="configuration-queryflag">
        <list>
            <li>
                <a href="QueryFlag-Create-Templates.topic">Create at least one template</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
                Make sure the template's data source is available in the current project, in the <control>Database</control> tool window.
            </li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Run a query" id="run-query">
        <procedure title="Run a template on selected text" id="steps-sequence">
            <step>
                In the editor, select the value you want to search for.
            </step>
            <step>
                Right-click the selection and select <ui-path>Query Flag in DB | &lt;template name&gt;</ui-path>.
                <!-- planned-image src="queryflag_editor_context_menu.png" alt="Editor context menu with Query Flag in DB expanded, showing the saved templates" -->
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>
            The IDE shows the results as for any query that you run from a query console, for example in the <control>Services</control> tool window.
        </p>
        <!-- planned-image src="queryflag_overview.png" alt="QueryFlag run: the selected value in the editor and the matching rows in the Services tool window" -->
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="What happens when you run a template" id="what-happens">
        <list type="decimal">
            <li>
                QueryFlag replaces each <code>&lt;QUERY_FLAG_TOKEN&gt;</code> token in the template with the selected text, without double quotes
                (see <a anchor="selection"/>).
            </li>
            <li>It creates a new query console for the template's data source and writes the query into it.</li>
            <li>It runs the query with the IDE's default query execution settings.</li>
        </list>
        <p>
            The query console does not open in the editor by default.
            To see and edit the query that ran, select <control>Open console editor</control> in the
            <a href="QueryFlag-Settings.topic">QueryFlag settings</a>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="How QueryFlag reads the selection" id="selection">
        <list>
            <li>
                Double quotes are removed, so selecting <code>"dark-mode"</code> with or without its quotes gives <code>dark-mode</code>.
                Put the quotes the query needs in the template; see <a href="QueryFlag-Create-Templates.topic" anchor="token-rules"/>.
            </li>
            <li>
                Everything else is kept as it is, including spaces, line breaks, and single quotes.
            </li>
            <li>
                QueryFlag reads the selection in editor tabs that show a file, including query consoles.
                In other editors, such as the diff viewer, the selection counts as empty.
            </li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Run a template without a selection" id="blank-selection">
        <p>
            The <control>Query Flag in DB</control> menu is available even when nothing is selected.
            By default, QueryFlag does not run a template when the selection is empty or contains only spaces.
            It shows the warning "Query with blank text is disable, skipping execution. Check QueryFlag preference to enable it."
        </p>
        <!-- planned-image src="queryflag_blank_selection_warning.png" alt="Warning notification when running QueryFlag without a selection" -->
        <p>
            To run templates with an empty value, select <control>Allow blank Text</control> in the
            <a href="QueryFlag-Settings.topic">QueryFlag settings</a>.
            A partial-match template such as <code>LIKE '%&lt;QUERY_FLAG_TOKEN&gt;%'</code> then matches every row that has a value in that column.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <seealso>
        <category ref="related">
            <a href="QueryFlag-Create-Templates.topic"/>
